# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a strand whose per-strand safepoint_budget_remaining reaches 0
#         yields back to the scheduler (soft yield) and is re-enqueued READY
#         rather than killed; it resumes on the next scheduler turn.
#
# blocked: per-strand soft-yield-and-resume is a scheduler internal, verified
#          by C unit tests, not a chk target.  Surfacing the yield/resume
#          boundary as two cross-turn observables in a golden-diff fixture
#          would require freezing test-only host-observation hooks (an
#          enqueue-without-drive primitive plus a mid-flight per-strand
#          emitter) into the v1.0 embedding API — rejected on API-minimalism
#          grounds.  The soft-yield-and-resume path is covered by
#          tests/unit/test_dispatch_loop.c (per_strand_budget_zero_causes_soft_yield,
#          zero_strand_budget_forces_mid_step_yield).  If runtime per-strand
#          budget control is ever exposed, it belongs in the reserved v1.x
#          scheduler-class abstraction (USchedClass / sched_strand_init attrs),
#          not a one-off setter.  Disposition: covered-by-unit-tests; not a chk target.
# matrix-row: scheduler-budget
